  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:honest-length-frontier",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Uniformly over \\(d\\le c_{\\epsilon}n\\log(en)\\), \\(\\mathsf W^*_{n,d,\\epsilon,M,\\alpha}\\asymp_{\\epsilon,\\alpha}M\\min\\{1,n^{-1/2}+d/[n\\log(en)]\\}\\). The exact-real interval \\(\\widehat C^{\\mathrm{HL}}\\) attains the upper inequality, and for every \\(0<\\delta_{\\mathrm{num}}\\le r_{n,d,M}\\) so does its certified outward-rounded implementation \\(\\widehat C^{\\mathrm{HL}}_{\\delta_{\\mathrm{num}}}\\), up to the same constant order.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "\\(d\\)",
      "\\(c_{\\epsilon}\\)",
      "\\(n\\)",
      "\\(\\epsilon\\)",
      "\\(M\\)",
      "\\(\\alpha\\)",
      "\\(\\mathsf W^*_{n,d,\\epsilon,M,\\alpha}\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat C^{\\mathrm{HL}}\\)",
      "\\(\\delta_{\\mathrm{num}}\\)",
      "\\(r_{n,d,M}\\)",
      "\\(\\widehat C^{\\mathrm{HL}}_{\\delta_{\\mathrm{num}}}\\)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:minimax-honest-length",
      "def:frontier-scale",
      "thm:global-honest-upper",
      "thm:same-class-testing-converse",
      "prop:certified-finite-precision-implementation"
    ],
    "justification": "The same-class lower bound is proved, and a separate proposition now records the best closed fallback bracket.",
    "gap": "The rate-matching upper inequality and its certified implementation still depend on the unresolved global calibration theorem.",
    "consumer": "It remains the target sample-size and alphabet-size benchmark for honest saturated adjustment.",
    "proof_tex": "By \\(thm:global\\text{-}honest\\text{-}upper\\), the particular measurable\ninterval \\(\\widehat C^{\\mathrm{HL}}\\) is admissible in the infimum defining\n\\(\\mathsf W^*_{n,d,\\epsilon,M,\\alpha}\\).  Therefore\n\\[\n \\mathsf W^*_{n,d,\\epsilon,M,\\alpha}\n \\le \\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal P_{d,\\epsilon,M}}\n E_{Q_P^{(n)}}[|\\widehat C^{\\mathrm{HL}}|]\n \\le C_{\\epsilon,\\alpha}r_{n,d,M}.\n\\tag{1}\n\\]\nConversely, \\(thm:same\\text{-}class\\text{-}testing\\text{-}converse\\) applies\nto every interval admitted by \\(def:minimax\\text{-}honest\\text{-}length\\), so\ntaking first its supremum over \\(P\\) and then the infimum over intervals gives\n\\[\n \\mathsf W^*_{n,d,\\epsilon,M,\\alpha}\n \\ge c_{\\epsilon,\\alpha}r_{n,d,M}.\n\\tag{2}\n\\]\nSubstitution of \\(def:frontier\\text{-}scale\\) into (1)--(2) proves the displayed\nequivalence uniformly on \\(d\\le c_\\epsilon n\\log(en)\\).  Finally,\n\\(prop:certified\\text{-}finite\\text{-}precision\\text{-}implementation\\) gives\ncoverage of the outward-rounded interval and adds at most\n\\(2\\delta_{\\mathrm{num}}\\le2r_{n,d,M}\\) to its expected length.  Thus it has\nthe same constant-order upper bound.",
